# ─── Models and binary artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Trained models are large and mostly regenerable. IMPORTANT EXCEPTION: the
# saved stacking ensemble is required to reproduce the ACI / calibration-
# diversity results (fix-reg/task_oof_and_probit.py loads it), so it is
# force-included below. If it is not already tracked, add it deliberately:
#   git add -f fix-reg/models/full_chain_stacking.pkl
*.pkl
*.pt
*.pth
*.joblib
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.onnx
*.cbm
*.sqlite
*.db
!fix-reg/models/full_chain_stacking.pkl

# Training telemetry
catboost_info/
mlruns/
lightning_logs/
wandb/
runs/

# ─── Large raw datasets (public, re-downloadable) ─────────────────────────────
# Fetched by the domain scripts and far too large for git:
#   data/domains/noaa/                 ~263 MB  NOAA Storm Events yearly CSVs
#   data/domains/uci_diabetes_130.csv   ~19 MB  UCI Diabetes 130-US Hospitals
# Both are public; exact sources are documented in
# fix-reg/multidomain_findings.md. The small derived panel IS tracked so the
# climate domain can be re-run without re-downloading 263 MB.
data/domains/noaa/
data/domains/uci_diabetes_130.csv
!data/domains/noaa_panel.csv

